<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the notarized macOS editor, applied by the "Sign and notarize
  the macOS bundle" step in `.github/workflows/build-engine.yml`.

  Apple will only notarize a binary signed with the hardened runtime, and the
  hardened runtime turns on protections this engine specifically cannot live
  with. Each key below buys back exactly one of them; nothing here is
  precautionary, and nothing should be added without the same kind of reason.

  Not used by a local `cargo renzora dist`, which seals the bundle ad-hoc. The
  hardened runtime is not in force there, so there is nothing to buy back.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      The load-bearing one. Library validation restricts a process to loading
      code signed by its own team, and the whole native-plugin design is the
      opposite of that: the editor stages an SDK, compiles a plugin or a `.rs`
      script on the user's machine, and `dlopen`s the result. rustc's linker
      signs that ad-hoc, under no team at all — so with validation on, a
      perfectly notarized editor would build plugins all day and load none of
      them. Marketplace plugins are the same story with someone else's team.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
